    "chunk_size_bytes": 2006,
    "chunk_text": "BE it therefore enacted by the Parliament of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows :\u2014\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the PiliyandalaDharmashastrodaya Piriven Viharastha SanwardhanaSabhawa (Incorporation) Act, No. of 2010.\n\nIncorporationof thePiliyandalaDharma-shastrodayaPririvenViharasthaSanwardhanaSabhawa.\n\nPiliyandala Dharmashastrodaya Piriven Viharastha\n\nSanwardhana Sabhawa (Incorporation)2\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n3.The general objects for which the Corporation isconstituted are hereby declared to be\u2014\n\n(a)to maintain buildings owned by the Viharaya andto construct and maintain new buildings as andwhen necessary;\n\n(b)to conduct activities for the promotion of religiousfavour among Buddhists and the people of the area;\n\n(c)to promte, encourage and assist in, activities for thespiritual, cultural, social and physical welfare of itsmembers;\n\n(d)to safeguard and propagate Buddhism ;\n\n(e)to establish monasteries and forest hermitages andto provide environmental facilities appropriate forthe accomplishment of its objects ;\n\n(f)to ordain youth with the requisite qualificationsand religious devotion and to provide them withthe four requisites;\n\n(g)to preserve and disseminate the TheravadhiBuddhist philosophy and way of life;\n\n(h)to maintain friendly relations with other BuddhistOrganisations, in and outside Sri Lanka;\n\n(i)to open a hospital for sick monks and to providemedical facilities to all the monks leading amonastic life;\n\n(j)to teach the dhamma and the Vinaya to monks, totrain them in yoga exercises and to make themproficient in Pali, Sinhala and oriental and westernlanguages;\n\nGeneralObjects oftheCorporation.\n\n3Piliyandala Dharmashastrodaya Piriven Viharastha\n\nSanwardhana Sabhawa (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n(k)to establish dhamma schools, and to provideknowledge of the dhamma to the youngergeneration ;\n\n(l)to communicate the message contained in theteachings of the Buddha and to propagate Buddhistculture with a view to promoting world peace;"
