    "chunk_text": "(e) organizing and conducting programmes forempowering deprived families while minimizingpoverty and introducing self employmentgenerating projects while helping sickly personsin low income families and assisting during specialevents in those families such as funerals andweddings;\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n35\n\nMaithripala Senanayake Foundation (Incorporation)3\n\n5\n\n20\n\n10\n\n15\n\n25\n\n30\n\n(g) establishing a legal assistance service to help thosewho are in need of legal services;\n\n(h) to assist the citizens by intervening when assistanceis requested by them to protect their rights underthe fundamental rights and human rights assertedin the Constitution of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka and the human rightsproclaimed in the UN charter of human rights;\n\n(i) organizing workshops to enhance professional andintellectual skills of the youth, while providingeducation in the field of modern science andtechnology and acclaiming novel efforts of thosewho are engaged in the field;\n\n(j) creating training opportunities for the youth in thefields that have good demand in the employmentmarket such as technical, construction, informationtechnology, computer and mobile phones, andregistering them after the conclusion of trainingand directing them towards potential local andoverseas employment opportunities;\n\n(k) encouraging those who are engaged in the fields offine arts such as painting, sculpturing, carving,music, dance, plays, tele-dramas and films whileproviding media facilities for the acclamation oftheir achievements;\n\n(l) creating skilled athletes to achieve national andinternational goals by launching a programmenamed \u201cKreeda Saviya\u201d and working to preservetraditional sports while organizing traditional sportsevents to conserve them as national heritages; and\n\n(m) training and establishing an Elite Task Force fordisaster management consisting of hundred capableyouth that would provide active intervention duringregional as well as national level outbreaks."
