    "chunk_text": "2.For the avoidance of doubts it is hereby declaredthat the provisions of the Acts specified in the First Scheduleto this Act shall be deemed to have no application in respectof the enactments specified in the Second Schedule to thisAct, and specifically in relation to the provisions dealingwith administration of the Acts and its application,membership, contributions and mode of collection ofcontributions.\n\n(2) Upon the Resolution seeking to amend the FirstSchedule and the Second Schedule being approved byParliament in accordance with the Standing Orders ofParliament, the Secretary to the Ministry of the Ministershall publish a Notification in the Gazette setting out thecontent of the Resolution in such manner as indicates theamendment made to the Schedule.\n\nAvoidance ofdoubts.\n\nAmendmentof FirstSchedule byResolution ofParliament.\n\nPensions (Consequential Provisions)2\n\n4.In the event of an inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text to prevail.\n\nFIRST SCHEDULE\n\nNAME OF ENACTMENT\n\n1. Employees\u2019 Provident Fund, Act, No. 15 of 1958.\n\n2. Payment of Gratuity Act, No. 12 of 1983.\n\nSECOND SCHEDULE\n\nNAME OF ENACTMENT\n\n1. Employees\u2019 Pension Benefits Act, No. of 2011.\n\n2. Overseas Employees\u2019 Pension Benefits Act, No. of\n\n2011.\n\nSinhala textto prevail incase ofinconsistency.\n\n3Pensions (Consequential Provisions)\n\nAnnual subscription of English Bills and Acts of the Parliament Rs. 885 (Local), Rs. 1,180(Foreign), Payable to the SUPERINTENDENT, GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, DEPARTMENT OFGOVERNMENT INFORMATION, NO. 163, KIRULAPONA MAWATHA, POLHENGODA, COLOMBO 05 before 15thDecember each year in respect of the year following."
