    "chunk_text": "THE GAZETTE OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPart II of June 08, 2012\n\nSUPPLEMENT\n\n(Issued on 11. 06. 2012)\n\nNINETEENTH AMENDMENT TOTHE CONSTITUTION\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nTo be presented in Parliament by Hon. Wijeyadasa Rajapakshe, M. P. for Colombo District\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 3.00Postage : Rs. 5.00\n\n(Private Member\u2019s Bill)\n\n2\u2014PL 002952\n\nto amend the Constitution of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n1Nineteenth Amendment to the Constitution\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE CONSTITUTION OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA.\n\nWHEREAS the Constitution of the Democrtic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka has guaranteed and assured to protectand foster the Buddha Sasana and the rights of all otherreligions:\n\nWHEREAS it has become a timely need to enact provisionsinto the Constitution for the purpose of maintenance andpreservation of religious dignity and holiness with a view toachieving of unity and concord of the Nation:\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Nineteenth Amendmentto the Constitution.\n\n2. The Article 91 of the Constitution be amended byinserting the following:\u2014\n\n\u201c91(1) (d) (xiii) a priest of any religion\u201d.\n\n3.This amendment shall come into operation soon afterthe expiry or the dissolution of the seventh Parliament.\n\n4.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nShort title.\n\nAmendmentof Article 91of theConstitution.\n\nPreamble.\n\nDate ofoperation ofAmendment.\n\nSinhala textto prevail incase ofinconsistency.\n\nNineteenth Amendment to the Constitution2"
  },
