    "chunk_text": "Marriage Registration (Amendment)2\n\n4.Section 34 of the principal enactment is herebyamended by the repeal of subsection (5) of that section andthe substitution therefor, of the following subsection :\u2014\n\n5.Section 38 of the principal enactment is herebyamemded by the repeal of subsection (2) of that section andthe substitution therefor, of the following subsection :\u2014\n\n\u201c(2) In case the female party belongs to a class otherthan that described in the preceding subsection or is inthe opinion of the District Registrar, not entitled to thebenefits of that subsection, it shall be lawful for the DistrictRegistrar upon the application of one of the parties to theindented marriage, and which application shall beaccompanied by a receipt issued by the District Registrarin proof of payment of a sum of rupees three thousandfive hundred or such othe amount as may be prescribedby the Minister from time to time, to issue a licenseempowering a registrar to solemnize the marriage at suchplace and hour as the parties my prefer and as they may benamed in this licence.\u201d.\n\n6.Section 51 of the principal enactment is herebyamemded by the repeal of subsection (2) of that section andthe substitution therefor, of the following subsection :\u2014\n\n\u201c(2) The applicant shall pay in respect of every writtenapplication and in respect of every certified copy orcertified extract thereof such amount as may be prescribedby the Minister from time to time.\u201d.\n\nAmendmentof section 34of theprincipalenactment.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\nAmendmentof section 38of theprincipalenactment.\n\n35\n\nAmendmentof section 51of theprincipalenactment.\n\n3Marriage Registration (Amendment)\n\n7.Section 62 of the principal enactment is herebyamended in subsection (1) of that section by the substitutionfor the words \u201cthe fees enumerated in the second schedule\u201dof the words \u201cthe fees enumerated in the second schedulewhich may be prescribed by the Minister from time totime,\u201d."
