    "chunk_text": "4.(1) The affairs of the Corporation shall subject to theother provisions of this Act and the rules in force for the timebeing of the Corporation, be administered by a SuperiorCommittee consisting of the Chairman / Director General,Administrative Secretary, Senior Vice Chairman, ViceChairman, Regional Organizer and Deputy Director Generalto be elected in accordance with such rules in force for thetime being of the Corporation.\n\nManagementof the affairsof theCorporation.\n\n4Sri Lanka Cultural Foundation for the Buildingof Culture and Morals (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n(3) The successor so nominated shall consist of themembers of the Superior Commettee of the Foundationholding office on the day preceding the date ofcommencement of this Act.\n\n5.Subject to the provisions of this Act and any otherwritten law the Corporation shall have the powers\u2014\n\n(a)to borrow and raise money for the purpose of theCorporation;\n\n(b)to make, draw, accept, discount, endorse, negotiate,buy, sell and issue bills of exchange, cheques,promissory Notes and other negotiable instrumentsand to open, operate, maintain and close bankaccounts;\n\n(c)to invest any funds which are not immediatelyrequired for the purposes of the Corporation in suchmanner as the Superior Committee may think fit;\n\n(d)to solicit and receive subscription, grants, donationsand gifts of all kinds;\n\n(e)to enter into agreements or contracts with anyperson, company or body of persons;\n\n(f)to undertake, accept, exeute, perform and administerany lawful trusts and conditions affection anymovable or immovable property;\n\n(g)to appoint, employ, dismiss or terminate the servicesof officers and servants of the Corporation and topay them such salaries, allowances and gratuitiesas may be determind by the Corporation;\n\nGeneralPowers of theCorporation.\n\n5Sri Lanka Cultural Foundation for the Buildingof Culture and Morals (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n(h)to train personnel in Sri Lanka or abroad forpurposes of the Corporation; and"
