    "chunk_text": "GeneralPowers of theCorporation.\n\n5Sri Lanka Cultural Foundation for the Buildingof Culture and Morals (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n(h)to train personnel in Sri Lanka or abroad forpurposes of the Corporation; and\n\n6.(1) It shall be lawful for the Corporation from time totime at any general meeting and by a majority of not lessthan two-thirds of the members present and voting to makerules not inconsistant with the provisions of this Act or anyother written law for all or any of the following matters\u2014\n\n(a)classification of membership, fees payable by eachclass of members, their admission, withdrawal orexpulsion or resignation;\n\n(b)election of the Superior Committee, the resignationfrom, vacation of, or removal from office of theoffice bearers and powers, duties and conduct ofthe Superior Committee;\n\n(c)appointment, dismissal, powers, dities, functionsand conduct of the various officers, agents andservants of the Corporation;\n\n(d)the procedure to be observed or the summoningand holding of meetings of the Superior Committee,the Corporation or any sub-Committee thereof,filling of vacancies, notices and agendas of suchmeetings, the quorm therefore and the conduct ofbusiness thereat;\n\n(e)the qualifications and disqualification formembership in the Superior Committee of theCorporation;\n\n(f)the administration and management of the propertyof the Corporation; and\n\nRules of theCorporation.\n\n6Sri Lanka Cultural Foundation for the Buildingof Culture and Morals (Incorporation)\n\n(g)generally for the management of the affairs of theCorporation and the accomplishment of its objects.\n\n(2) The rules of the Foundation in force on the precedingdate of commencement of this Act shall, in so far as they arenot inconsistent with the provisions of this Act or any otherwritten law be deemed to be the rules of the Corporation andmay be amended, altered, added to, or rescinded at a likemeeting and in like manner as rules made under thissection."
