    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nINSTITUTE OF POLICY STUDIES OF SRI LANKA(AMENDMENT)\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Bill No. 269]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by the Minister of Finance and Planningon 09th October, 2013\n\n(Published in the Gazette on September 23, 2013)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nto amend the Institute of Policy Studies of Sri LankaAct, No. 53 of 1988\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 3.00Postage : Rs. 5. 00\n\n2-2d\n\n2-PL 007667 \u20141,100 (10/2013)\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2: This clause amends paragraph (c) of section 7 of the Institute of Policy Studiesof Sri Lanka Act, No. 53 of 1988, and the legal effect of the section as amended is to enablethe Governor of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka to nominate a representative to the Board ofGovernors of the Institute.\n\n1Institute of Policy Studies ofSri Lanka (Amendment)\n\n2\u2014PL 007573\u2014 425 (09/2013)\n\nShort title.\n\n5\n\n10\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 34/2012\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE INSTITUTE OF POLICY STUDIES OF SRI LANKAACT, NO. 53 OF 1988\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Institute of PolicyStudies of Sri Lanka (Amendment) Act, No. of 2013.\n\n2.Section 7 of the Institute of Policy Studies ofSri Lanka Act, No. 53 of 1988 is hereby amended by therepeal of paragraph (c) of that section, and the substitutiontherefor of the following paragraph:\u2014\n\n\u201c(c)the Governor of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka or anofficer nominated by the Governor;\u201d\n\n3.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nAmendmentof Section 7ofAct,No.53 of1988.\n\nSinhala textto prevail incase ofinconsistency.\n\n2Institute of Policy Studies ofSri Lanka (Amendment)"
