    "chunk_size_bytes": 2030,
    "chunk_text": "BE it therefore enacted by the Parliament of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Study Centre for theAdvancement of Technology and Social Welfare(Incorporation) Act, No. of 2013.\n\nIncorporationof the StudyCentre for theAdvancementofTechnologyand SocialWelfare.\n\n2Study Centre for the Advancement ofTechnology and Social Welfare (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n3.The general objects for which the Corporation isconstituted are hereby declared to be\u2014\n\n(a)to initiate the establishment of favourable culturalheritage among Sri Lankans and to revive the SriLankan culture among the Sri Lankan community,living in other countries including Australia;\n\n(b)to enlighten the Sri Lankans and internationalcommunity residing in other countries includingAustralia about the Sri Lankan framework relatingto the spheres of culture, economy, politics andsport;\n\n(c)to discuss and take necessary action regarding theissues and other responsibilities which affect theSri Lankans, living in other countries includingAustralia;\n\n(d)to assist the Sri Lankans residing around the worldto exchange the education, the development andthe technology and maintain close ties with the SriLankans for the socio economic and culturaldevelopment;\n\n(e)to organize social welfare activities for the benefitof Sri Lankans, specially the aged, youth, womenand non-privileged groups and to assist theinstitutions and community needs in Sri Lanka,Australia and other countries;\n\n(f)to introduce the modern technology, arts, modernmanagement and busness skills to Sri Lankans,residing in Sri Lanka, Australia and other countries,to organize educational programmes continuouslyand also assist in professional improvement;\n\n(g)to provide advices and assistance to the supply ofbasic needs of the Sri Lankans and students comingto Australia and other countries;\n\nGeneralobjects of theCorporation.\n\n3Study Centre for the Advancement ofTechnology and Social Welfare (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30"
  },
