    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nPresented by the Prime Minister and Minister of Buddha Sasana andReligious Affairs on 21st March, 2014\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 11.00Postage : Rs. 5.00\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Bill No. 292]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n(Published in the Gazette on March 10, 2014)\n\nVALUE ADDED TAX (AMENDMENT)\n\nto amend the Value Added Tax Act, No. 14 of 2002\n\n2\u2014PL 008090\u2014525 (03/2014)\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2: This Clause amends section 3 of the Value Added Tax Act, No.14 of 2002(hereinafter referred to as the principal enactment) and the legal effect of that section asamended is to reduce the threshold of the liability of the wholesale and retail trade fromRs. 500 Million to Rs. 250 Million and related matters.\n\nClause 3: This Clause amends section 8 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof that section as amended is to limit the exemption granted to the wholesale or retailbusiness subject to certain conditions.\n\nClause 4: This Clause amends section 10 of the principal enactment and is consequentialto the amendment made to section 3 of the principal enactment.\n\nClause 5: This section amends section 20 of the principal enactment and the legaleffect of that section as amended is to provide for the avoidance of the issue of tax invoiceson deemed liability referred to in section 8 of the principal enactment.\n\nClause 6: This Clause amends section 22 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof that section as amended is to provide for matters in the case where long term and generalinsurance businesses are segregated by the persons carrying on both long term insurancebusiness and general insurance business,and to allow any bank or finance company toclaim the unabsorbed input credit where any acquisition or merger of such bank orfinance company takes place."
