    "chunk_size_bytes": 1978,
    "chunk_text": "Clause 6: This Clause amends section 22 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof that section as amended is to provide for matters in the case where long term and generalinsurance businesses are segregated by the persons carrying on both long term insurancebusiness and general insurance business,and to allow any bank or finance company toclaim the unabsorbed input credit where any acquisition or merger of such bank orfinance company takes place.\n\nClause 8: This Clause amends section 25D of the principal enactment and is consequentialto the amendment made to section 25C of the principal amendment.\n\nClause 9: This Clause amends section 40 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof that section as amended is to expand the present preferential claims of default tax fromone year to five years.\n\nClause 10: This Clause amends section 71 of the principal enactment and the legaleffect of that section as amended is to reduce the contribution to the VAT refund fund bythe Director- General of Customs on importation of goods from 10% to 6%.\n\nClause 11: This Clause amends section 83 of the principal enactment and the legaleffect of that section as amended is to expand the definition of \u201cinternational transportation\u201d.\n\nClause 12: This Clause amends PART II of the First Schedule to the principal enactmentin order to add new exemptions and to restrict exemptions granted to certain items.\n\nClause 13: This Clause specifies the change of certain designations in keeping with thechanges made to such designations in the Service Minute of the Inland Revenue Service.\n\nValue Added Tax(Amendment)1\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n2\u2014PL 008031\u2014425 (03/2014)\n\n20\n\nL.D. \u2013 O. 4/2014\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE VALUE ADDED TAX ACT, NO. 14 OF 2002\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:-\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Value Added Tax(Amendment) Act, No. of 2014 and shall be deemed to havecome into operation on January 1, 2014."
  },
