    "chunk_text": "THE GAZETTE OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPart II of August 01, 2014\n\nSUPPLEMENT\n\n(Issued on 04.08.2014)\n\nLOCAL AUTHORITIES FILLING OF VACANCIES(SPECIAL PROVISIONS) (AMENDMENT)\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nto amend the Local Authorities Filling of Vacancies (Special Provisions)Act, No. 30 of 2013\n\nOrdered to be published by the Minister of Local Government andProvincial Councils\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 3.00Postage : Rs. 5.00\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2 : This clause amends section 2 of the Local Authorities Filling of Vacancies(Special Provisions) Act, No. 30 of 2013, by the repeal of the proviso to that section and itis consequential to the amendments made to subsection (4) of section 66B of the LocalAuthorities Elections Ordinance (Chapter 262) and the legal effect due to such repeal will beto revert back to the procedure followed by the Municipal Council, Urban Council orPradeshiya Sabha, prior to such amendment when re-submitting a budget or supplementarybudget to the Municipal Council, Urban Council or Pradeshiys Sabha, as the case may be.\n\n1Local Authorities Filling of Vacancies(Special Provisions) (Amendment)\n\nShort titleand date ofoperation.5\n\n10\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 3/2014\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE LOCAL AUTHORITIES FILLING OF VACANCIES(SPECIAL PROVISIONS) ACT, NO. 30 OF 2013\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Local Authorities Fillingof Vacancies (Special Provisions) (Amendment) Act, No. of2014 and shall come into operation on such date as theMinister may appoint by Order published in the Gazette.\n\n2.Section 2 of the Local Authorities Filling ofVacancies (Special Provisions) Act, No. 30 of 2013 is herebyamended by the repeal of the proviso to that section.\n\n3.In the event of any inconsistency between theSinhala and Tamil texts of this Act, Sinhala text shall prevail."
  },
