    "chunk_size_bytes": 1992,
    "chunk_text": "(2) A person shall not sell, offer for sale,supply, distribute or store a packet, package orcarton containing tobacco products unless astatement containing the tar and nicotinecontent and the health warnings are displayedconspicuously in legible print on the topsurface area of both front and back sides ofevery packet, package or carton containingthe tobocco product, as provided for insubsection (1).\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n\u201cProhibitionof themanufacture,sale, importetc. oftobaccoproductswithouthealthwarnings anda label or astatement oftar andnicotinecontent.\n\nShort titleand date ofoperation.\n\n30\n\nNational Authority on Tobacco and Alcohol(Amendment)2\n\n(3) Any person who contravenes theprovisions of this section shall commit anoffence and upon conviction after summarytrial by a Magistrate be liable to animprisonment of either description for a termnot exceeding one year or to a fine notexceeding rupees fifty thousand or to both suchfine and imprisonment.\u201d.\n\n3.The following new section is hereby insertedimmediately after Section 34 of the principal enactment andshall have effect as section 34A of the principal enactment:\u2014\n\n34A. (1) A manufacturer or an importer ofcigarettes and other tobacco products shallcause to be printed the health warning referredto in section 34(1), covering an area of eightyper centum of the top surface area (principledisplay area) of both front and back sides ofevery packet, package or carton containingcigarettes and other tobacco products.\n\n(2) A foresaid health warnings shall indicatethe health hazards and the harmful effectscaused by the usage of tobocco products, asmay be prescribed.\n\n(3) The health warning on the front and backsides of the packet, package or carton shalldefer from each other.\n\n(4) Where a manufacturer manufacturesmore than one brand of cigarettes and othertobaccoe products, the manufacturer shallensure that two different brands manufacturedby such manufacturer shall not bear the samehealth warning, simultaneously."
