    "chunk_text": "THE GAZETTE OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPart II of May 22, 2015\n\nSUPPLEMENT\n\n(Issued on 25. 05. 2015)\n\nTWENTY FIFTH AMENDMENT TOTHE CONSTITUTION\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nTo be presented in Parliament by Hon. Rajiva Wijesinha M. P.\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 16.00Postage : Rs. 15.00\n\n(Private Member\u2019s Bill)\n\nto amend the Constitution of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n1Twenty Fifth Amendment to the Constitution\n\n5\n\n10\n\n2\u2014PL 009042\u2014325 (05/2015)\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE CONSTITUTION OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA.\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Twenty FifthAmendment to the Constitution.\n\n2.Delete clauses 10 to 17 of the Constitution andreplace with the followings:\u2014\n\n10. (1) Every person is entitled to freedomof thought, conscience and religion, includingthe freedom to have or to adopt a religion orbelief of his choice.\n\n(2) No restrictions shall be placed on theexercise of the fundamental right declared andrecognized by this Article.\n\n10A. (1) Every person has inherent dignityand the right to have his or her dignityrespected and protected.\n\n(2) No restrictions shall be placed on theright declared and recognized by this Article.\n\n10B. (1) Every person has inherent right tolife and no person shall be arbitraily deprivedof life.\n\n(2) No person shall be punished with death.\n\n(3) Every person against whom a setence ofdeath has been prounounced before the cominginto force of the Eighteenth Amendment to theConstitution, shall have such sentence\n\nShort title.\n\n15\n\n20\n\nFreedom ofthought,conscienceand religion.\n\nInherentright to life.\n\nRight tohumandignity.\n\n25\n\nTwenty Fifth Amendment to the Constitution2\n\ncommuted to one of rigorous imprisonment forlife.\n\n(4) No restrictions shall be placed on therigths declared and recognized by this Article."
