    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nNATION BUILDING TAX (AMENDMENT)\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Bill No. 3]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by the Minister of Finance on 22nd September, 2015\n\n(Published in the Gazette on March 30, 2015)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nto amend the Nation Building Tax Act, No. 9 of 2009\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 11.00Postage : Rs. 10.00\n\n2-2d\n\n2-\n\n2-PL 009235 \u2014475 (09/2015)\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2 : This clause amends section 3 of the Nation Building Tax Act, No. 9 of 2009(hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) and the legal effect of the section asamended is -\n\n(a)to introduce a fresh calculation method for the payment of tax, in respect of thesupply of financial services;\n\n(b)to impose liability on a person engaged in the business of real estate anddevelopment to pay tax for the income arising from such business; and\n\n(c)to exempt certain articles from the liability of the payment of tax.\n\nClause 3 : This clause amends section 6 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof the section as amended is to exclude a person other than a manufacturer to be entitledfor tax credit under this Act.\n\nClause 4 : This clause inserts a new section 6B in the principal enactment and facilitatesthe use of electronic communications or electronic records.\n\nClause 5 : This clause amends section 10 of the principal enactment and the legaleffect of the section as amended is to replace the definition of \u2018service\u2019.\n\nClause 6 : This clause amends the First Schedule to the principal enactment and thelegal effect of the said Schedule as amended is to revise the present criteria of exemptionrelating to certain articles.\n\nClause 7 : This clause specify dates on which certain provisions come into force."
