    "chunk_text": "2.From and after the date of commencement of thisAct, such and so many persons as now are members of the\u201cDhammadeepa Foundation\u201d (hereinafter referred to as the\u201cFoundation\u201d) or shall hereafter be admitted as members ofthe Corporation hereby constituted, shall be a bodycorporate, with perpetual succession under the name andstyle of the \u201cDhammadeepa Foundation\u201d (hereinafter referredto as \u201cthe Corporation\u201d) and by that name may sue and besued, with full power and authority to have and use a commonseal and to alter the same at its pleasure.\n\n3.The general objects for which the Corporation isconstituted are hereby declared to be:\u2014\n\nPreamble.\n\nShort title.\n\nIncorporationofDhammadeepaFoundation.\n\nGeneralobjects of theCorporation.\n\n30\n\nDhammadeepa Foundation (Incorporation)2\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(b)to carry on Buddhist services by safeguardingsecurity of Buddhism;\n\n(c)to do charitable services under different projects;\n\n(i)For a quality education;(ii)For economic development activies;(iii)Projects such as awarding of scholarship toeconomically backward students.\n\n(d)going to remote under developedvillages and providing them with various reliefafter identifying their difficulties;\n\n(e)after identifying threats to Buddhism and the nationand implementing steps to eradicate them.\n\n4.Subject to the provisions of this Act and any otherwritten law perform and execut the following:\u2014\n\n(a)to raise funds and receive grants, gifts or donations,in cash or kind and requesting subscriptions;\n\n(b)to acquire, in any manner whatsoever and hold,take of give on lease or hire, rent, sell or otherwisedispose of, any movable or immovable propertyand construct, maintain and alter any buildings orworks necessary or convenient for the business ofthe Corporation;\n\n(c)to open, operate and close bank accounts andborrow or raise money with or without security;\n\n(d)to invest any funds not immediately required forthe purpose of the Corporation in such manner asthe elected Executive Committee may determine."
