    "chunk_size_bytes": 1871,
    "chunk_text": "2.From and after the commencement of this Act, suchand so many persons as now are members of the \u201cSri LankaHira Foundation\u201d (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cFoundation\u201d)or shall hereafter be admitted as members of the Corporationhereby constituted shall be a body corporate (hereinafterreferred to as the \u201cCorporation\u201d) with perpetual succession,under the name and style of the \u201cSri Lanka Foundation\u201d andby that name may sue and be sued in all courts, with fullpower and authority to have and use a common seal andalter the same at its pleasure.\n\n(a)Working to protect and develop all rights of womenand children;\n\nIncorporationof theSri LankaHiraFoundation.\n\n2Sri Lanka Hira Foundation (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n(b)assist affected people in disaster situation to uplifttheir life-style and providing legal assistance forneedy vulnerable people;\n\n(c)protect cultural values;\n\n(d)giving assistance to develop worship places;\n\n(e)to promote peace, goodwill, understanding andcooperation among all communities and people ofSri Lanka;\n\n(f)to give assistance, prizes and scholarships to needyschool children to enable to continue theireducation, encourage them to attend schoolregularly, and assist them in their education;\n\n(g)to establish self-employment opportunities forunemployed citizens and to provide loans and toinaugurate various savings schemes;\n\n(h)to take necessary steps to promote artistic creations,sport skills and technical knowledge of schoolleavers and to set up vocational training centers aswell as give them assistance to peruse studies incomputer science and technology and to establishinstitutions to provide such studies;\n\n(i)to assist in the development of educational,religious, cultural, aesthetic and sports facilitieswithout any reference to race, religion or caste andto conduct various festivals and competitions;"
