    "chunk_text": "(2) The Corporation shall have the power to borrow orraise money necessary for the furtherance of its objects andto create, execute, grant or issue any mortgages, bonds orobligations to receive such money.\n\n4Sri Lanka Association for Fisheries andAquatic Resources (Incorporation)\n\nDebts due byand payableto theCorporation.\n\nSeal of theCorporation.\n\nPower tocharge feesandsubscriptions.\n\nSaving of therights of theRepublic andothers.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n8.The Corporation shall be able and capable in law tocharge\u2014\n\n(a) such fees as the Association may deem reasonablefor admission to any course or examinationconducted by the Association ;\n\n(b) fees for the election of persons to any class ofmembership of the Association ; and\n\n(c) such subscriptions and fees as the Association maydeem reasonable in respect of services provided bythe Corporation.\n\n9.All debts and liabilities of the Association existing atthe time of coming into operation of this Act shall be paid ordischarged by the Corporation, and all, debts due to, andsubscriptions, and fees payable to the Association shall bepaid to the Corporation for the purposes of this Act.\n\n10.The Corporation shall have the power to appointany Committee and to take such other steps as may be foundnecessary, from time to time, for the furtherance of its objects.\n\n11.The seal of the Corporation shall not be affixed toany instrument whatsoever except in the presence of suchpersons as the Committee shall authorize from time to timeby Standing Order, who shall sign their names to theinstrument in token of their presence, and such signing shallbe independent of the signing of any person as a witness.\n\n12.Nothing contained in this Act shall prejudice oraffect the rights of the Republic or any body politic orcorporate or of any other persons, except such as arementioned in this Act and those claiming by, from or underthem.\n\n13.In the event of any inconsistency between theSinhala and the Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shallprevail."
