    "chunk_text": "THE GAZETTE OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPart II of December 04, 2015\n\nSUPPLEMENT\n\n(Issued on 07. 12. 2015)\n\nDAYA SARANA DEVELOPMENT FOUNDATION (INCORPORATION)\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nto incorporate the Daya Sarana Development Foundation\n\nTo be presented in Parliament by Hon. (Dr.) Mrs. Thusitha WijemannaM. P. for Kegalle District\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 8.00Postage : Rs. 10.00\n\n(Private Member\u2019s Bill)\n\n1Daya Sarana Development Foundation (Incorporation)\n\nPreamble.\n\nShort title.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nAN ACT TO INCORPORATE THE DAYA SARANA DEVELOPMENTFOUNDATION\n\nWHEREAS a Foundation called and known as the\u201cDaya Sarana Development Foundation\u201d has beenestablished in Sri Lanka for the purpose of effectuallycarrying out and transacting all objects and mattersconnected with the said Foundation according to the rulesagreed to the members:\n\nAND WHEREAS the said Foundation has heretoforesuccessfully carried out and transacted several objectsand matters for which it was established and has applied tobe incorporated and it will be for the public advantage togrant the application:\n\nBE it therefore enacted by the Parliament of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Daya SaranaDevelopment Foundation (Incorporation) Act,No. of 2016.\n\n2.From and after the date of commencement of thisAct, such and so many persons as now are members of theDaya Sarana Development Foundation (hereinafter referredto as \u201cthe Foundation\u201d) or shall hereafter be admitted asnow are members of the Corporation hereby constituted,shall be a body corporate (hereinafter referred to as the\u201cCorporation\u201d) with perpetual succession under the nameand style of the \u201cDaya Sarana Development Foundation\u201d,and by that name may sue and be sued in all courts, with fullpower and authority to have and use a common seal and toalter the same at its pleasure."
  },
