    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Bill No. 45]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by the Minister of Justiceon 11th December, 2015\n\n(Published in the Gazette on November 09, 2015)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\n2-2d\n\n2-\n\nPrice : Rs. 3.00Postage : Rs. 10.00\n\nPENAL CODE (AMENDMENT)\n\nto amend the Penal Code (Chapter 19)\n\n2\u2014PL 009559\u2014475 (12/2015)\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2: This clause inserts new section 291c in the Penal Code (Chapter 19) and thelegal effect of the section is to make provision to convict and punish persons who cause orinstigate acts of violence or hostility which lead to religious, racial or communal disharmonybetween different racial or religious groups.\n\n1Penal Code (Amendment)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n2\u2014PL 009335\u2014425 (10/2015)\n\nShort title.\n\nL. D.\u2014O. 28/2015.\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE PENAL CODE (CHAPTER 19)\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Penal Code(Amendment) Act, No. of 2015.\n\n2.The following section is hereby inserted immediatelyafter section 291B of the Penal Code (Chapter 19) and shallhave effect as section 291C of that Code:\u2014\n\n291C. Whoever, by the use of words spoken,written or intended to be read, or by signs, orby visible representation, or otherwise, intendsto cause or attempts to cause or instigates orattempts to instigate, acts of violence orreligious, racial or communal disharmony, orfeelings of ill-will or hostility, betweencommunities or different classes of persons ordifferent racial or religious groups, shall bepunished with imprisonment of eitherdescription for a term which may extend totwo years.\u201d.\n\n3.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nInsertion ofnew section291C inChapter 19."
